    "task": "epitope-databases"
  },
  "task": "There is 10x-genomics single cell CellRanger data with RNA-seq and TCR-seq (contig annotations) data for blood (*B samples), tumor (*T samples) and normal tumor-adjacent tissue (*N samples) for different patients. Load the data, perform quality control. Combine all samples and keep only cells present in both the RNA-seq and TCR-seq data. Keep only alpha/beta T cells with at least one productive alpha and one productive beta chain and at most two of each. Annotate each cell with the IggyTop epitope database (scirpy ir.datasets.iggytop()): match by identical CDR3 amino-acid sequence, where a match on either the alpha or the beta chain, in either receptor pair, counts. When a cell matches several entries, assign the most frequent antigen species; label ties \"ambiguous\". Which antigen species is most common (by number of cells) in normal tissue? Excluding \"ambiguous\" and that species, which two antigen species are most common in tumor tissue (order does not matter)? Excluding \"ambiguous\", how many antigen species are assigned to more than 5 blood cells?"
}
